  "summary": "Iraqi art refers to all works of visual art originating from the geographical region of what is present day Iraq since ancient Mesopotamian periods.",
  "description": "Iraqi art refers to all works of visual art originating from the geographical region of what is present day Iraq since ancient Mesopotamian periods. Under the Abbasid Caliphate, Baghdad was a literary and artistic center of Arab world. Its artistic traditions suffered at the hands of the Mongol invasion of the 13th century. Under Ottoman rule in the 16th century, Baghdad was known for its Ottoman miniature painting. In the 20th century, an art revival, produced many notable poets, painters and sculptors who contributed to the inventory of public artworks, especially in Baghdad.",
